### Manual API checks (VS Code "REST Client" extension). No real tokens are stored here:
### run the login request, copy the access_token from the response and paste it below.
@base = http://127.0.0.1:5000/api
@token = PASTE_ACCESS_TOKEN_HERE

### Register
POST {{base}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{ "username": "demo", "email": "demo@example.com", "password": "change-me-123" }

### Login
POST {{base}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "demo@example.com", "password": "change-me-123" }

### Create a project
POST {{base}}/projects/
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "title": "My project", "description": "demo", "research_field": "NLP" }

### List papers of project 1
GET {{base}}/projects/1/papers
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Upload a PDF to project 1 (use the Papers tab in the UI, or curl):
### curl -H "Authorization: Bearer <token>" -F "file=@paper.pdf" http://127.0.0.1:5000/api/projects/1/papers

### Which embedder is active?
GET {{base}}/nlp/status
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Ask (extractive answer with citations + verification)
POST {{base}}/projects/1/ask
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "question": "What problem does the paper address?" }

### Idea analysis
POST {{base}}/projects/1/idea
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "idea": "Describe a proposed research idea here" }

### Overlap check
POST {{base}}/projects/1/overlap
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "text": "Paste a paragraph to compare with the uploaded papers." }

### Retrieval evaluation on YOUR labelled queries (smoke test unless the set is large)
POST {{base}}/projects/1/evaluation/retrieval
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "k": 5, "queries": [ { "question": "example question", "relevant_paper_ids": [1] } ] }
